<title>NEW ZEALAND: Property for Industry buys Auck. property.</title>
<headline>Property for Industry buys Auck. property.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Property for Industry Ltd said on Wednesday it had bought an industrial property in Auckland for $8.2 million.</p>
<p>PFI Management Ltd General Manager David Jans said the property offered a strong initial yield of 11.9 percent under a long lease, with 14 1/2 years to expiry, with the protection of a full ratchet clause and Consumer Price Index growth at rent reviews.</p>
<p>It said the site of just under four hectares offered considerable scope for further development or future subdivision. -- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
